       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the maximum, so I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is too high.** The usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen is 800 mg. This order is 1,600 mg per dose, which is twice that.\n- **The daily total is too high.** 1,600 mg \u00d7 4 = **6,400 mg/day**. The usual prescription maximum is **3,200 mg/day**, so this is twice that too. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This might be a transcription error. Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total). This fits if \"1600\" was meant as the daily total.\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n3. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n4. Something else.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm and give me the clinical reason so I can add it to the order note. I'd also recommend checking with pharmacy first, since a dose this high will likely be flagged when they verify the order."
      }
     ],
