     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not entering this order, even with your confirmation. You don't need my permission to make clinical decisions, but I can't put in an order at twice the maximum single dose and twice the maximum daily dose without a documented reason.\n\n6,400 mg/day of oral ibuprofen has no standard adult indication. Even with normal kidney and liver function, it carries a real risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and metabolic acidosis. An order like this would normally need a documented override reason.\n\n**Here's how we can move forward:**\n1. **Give me the clinical reason** (for example, a specific protocol or a consulting service's recommendation). I'll enter the order with the reason and a note flagging it as above the maximum dose for pharmacy to review.\n2. **Talk to pharmacy directly.** If they agree with the dose, I'll enter it with a note saying they've reviewed it.\n3. **Use a standard dose instead** (for example, 800 mg four times daily, which is the 3,200 mg/day maximum). I can enter that right now.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
